{"name":"Cello","hex":"#3a4e5f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cello","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bowed bass instrument held between the knees."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["cellophane"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cello"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cello","blocks":[{"text":"The violoncello ( VY-ə-lən-CHEL-oh, Italian pronunciation: [vjolonˈtʃɛllo]), commonly abbreviated as cello ( CHEL-oh), is a medium-low pitched bowed string instrument of the violin family. Its four strings are usually tuned in perfect fifths: from low to high, C2, G2, D3 and A3. The viola's four strings are each an octave higher. Music for the cello is generally written in the bass clef; the tenor clef and treble clef are used for higher-range passages."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Cello_front_side.png/330px-Cello_front_side.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cello"},{"title":"Cello (web browser)","blocks":[{"text":"Cello is an early, discontinued graphical web browser for Windows 3.1; it was developed by Thomas R. Bruce of the Legal Information Institute at Cornell Law School. It was released as shareware in 1993. While other browsers ran on various Unix machines, Cello was the first web browser for Microsoft Windows, using the winsock system to access the Internet. In addition to the basic Windows, Cello worked on Windows NT 3.5 and with small modifications on OS/2."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a6/Cello_main_page.png/330px-Cello_main_page.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cello_(web_browser)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Range_cello.png/500px-Range_cello.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Range_cello.png/500px-Range_cello.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARange_cello.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Cello_study.jpg/500px-Cello_study.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Cello_study.jpg/1280px-Cello_study.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Cello_study.jpg/500px-Cello_study.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cello close-up","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACello_study.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Violoncello_open_strings.png/500px-Violoncello_open_strings.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Violoncello_open_strings.png/500px-Violoncello_open_strings.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cello open strings Playⓘ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVioloncello_open_strings.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Cello_and_a_bow.jpg/500px-Cello_and_a_bow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Cello_and_a_bow.jpg/1280px-Cello_and_a_bow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Cello_and_a_bow.jpg/500px-Cello_and_a_bow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cello close-up with a bow.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACello_and_a_bow.jpg"},{"srcset":"ht